// The 32 figures, each with a name and a judgment. Index = sum of 2^position of the moving cards (0 Stance, 1 Form, 2 Move, 3 Twist, 4 Constraint).
const FIGURES = [
["The Yoknapatawpha Principle","Do it here and now, with what you have, as Faulkner did with his South."],
["Recoupling With Reality","The moment you step out of words and habits and are there again."],
["Strangification","Make strange what is worn out. Its gentle version: nothing changes abruptly, everything shifts."],
["The Axes","What a life simplifies and hardens around: caring, teaching, being a parent, art."],
["The Fertility of Errors","Provoked errors, the grain of sand in the oyster, and accidents caught on the fly."],
["The Nonchalance of Masters","The ease of someone who knows their art, not the false ease of someone who prepared everything beforehand."],
["Things Hide When They Begin","What is born first shows what it shares with everything else. Its essence appears only in the middle."],
["The Second Disenchantment","Magellan reaches the Pacific and finds the ocean is even bigger. You change your life, and the new one is just as hard."],
["The Tiny Oddity","One repetition too many, one slightly wrong word: the literary equivalent of the slightly wrong note."],
["The Meta","The actor, the observer, the observer of the observer. Why does this give pleasure?"],
["Non-Documentary Realism","The real as it is, with almost nothing wrong."],
["The Symmetry Revolt","Doing the exact opposite of what you dislike: black instead of pink."],
["Level-Two Peril","Facing a great danger, you react fast, then stop and float: you have understood it hides a worse one."],
["The Deleuze Effect","A rain of seeds or tools that you find yourself using almost without noticing."],
["The Double Intense Feeling","Two extreme, opposite feelings at the same time."],
["The Fertility of Limits","The presence of banks gives the flow tenfold force."],
["Three Quarters of One's Strength","A successful work uses only three quarters of its author's strength, with the calm of cows lying in a meadow."],
["Positive Disenchantment","The truly disenchanted are calm and laugh, unlike the unhappy who scratch their wounds."],
["The Reading Grids","The photographer sees frames, the screenwriter stories, the engineer questions to fit together."],
["The Kingdoms","Power in one domain is worth nothing in another."],
["Doing Without Doing","A process diverted from its function."],
["The Absurd Princes","Those who have found their Axis, however tiny."],
["The Delicious Artifice","Being a spectator aware of being one, smiling at a well-made trick."],
["Incompleteness","Something is missing, with no precise object. Mapping it already helps a little."],
["The Perfect Moment, Spoiled","Every perfect moment is spoiled by something from outside, and it doesn't matter."],
["Conferred Value","Disappointing at first, then \"Sublime!\" once the papers have spoken."],
["The Lure","What attracts artificially, in order to deceive."],
["The Suze Theory","Keep a drink and a tin you don't like in the kitchen, to match your mood when life turns bitter."],
["Intimate Terror","The fixed idea of a misfortune that does arrive in the end, but by surprise, obliquely."],
["The Buoys","The projects that keep us busy like the tassel children grab at on the merry-go-round. When the buoy bursts, incompleteness returns."],
["The Waldgänger","In the world, without playing its game."],
["Long-Range Disillusions","A dream that obstacles made grow for years explodes on arrival; its debris finds its place in your personal puzzle."]];
